WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.830
- The slowdown in the Chinese economy

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.900
doesn't just hurt China.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.480
Some US companies do a
lot of business there

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.220
and have counted on the emerging economy

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.960
to help drive their profits.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.067
During the second quarter,

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:15.360
S&amp;P 500 companies
mentioned China 182 times.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.410
That was the fewest number

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.350
of times since the fourth quarter of 2021.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.690
But as the third quarter
earning season starts to heat up

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.523
in the US,

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:25.350
there are three big reasons
you're likely to hear a lot more

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.990
about China from American companies.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.540
First, companies that generate big chunks

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.640
of their revenue from
China are driving much

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.200
of the stock market's gains this year.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.630
The S&amp;P 500 index is weighted based

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.180
on how large each company in the index is.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.410
And in recent years,

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.480
tech companies have come to dominate.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.910
Companies like Tesla, Apple and NVIDIA

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.200
have been responsible for much

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.790
of the rise in the S&amp;P this year

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.400
and they all do a lot
of business in China.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.040
While only 7.5% of revenue for companies

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.200
in the SS&amp;P 500 comes from China,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.600
about 16% of revenue for companies

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.390
in the information technology
sector is China-based.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.730
For semiconductor companies like NVIDIA,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.280
27% of revenue originates there.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.320
And when the Chinese economy slows down,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.350
like it has this year, that
usually means Chinese businesses

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.180
and consumers buy less.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.863
That includes US products.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.560
Second, we've seen rising
tensions between the US and China

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.700
with both countries

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.133
recently unveiling new
restrictions on trade.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.880
Sources told my colleague
Yoko Kubota in September

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.830
that officials at central
government agencies

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.710
in China have been told
not to bring Apple's iPhone

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.850
to the office.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.920
And Beijing recently instituted a ban

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.960
on Chinese firms buying products

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.030
from Idaho-based chip maker Micron.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.100
The company said earlier
this year that the ban

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.770
could have a quote, "Double
digit percentage impact

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.300
on its total sales."

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.920
China has also ramped up bans

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.690
on foreigners leaving the country,

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.120
targeting bankers and executives.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.430
The US has also made things more difficult

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.800
for American companies
doing business in China,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.000
banning the sale of chips

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.580
and other tech equipment
to Chinese companies.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.070
NVIDIA's chief financial
officer recently said

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.890
that further restrictions on
sales to China would result

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.370
in a quote, "Permanent loss
for the US industry to compete

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.250
and lead in one of the
world's largest markets."

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.970
Third, the Chinese economy
slowdown is having a wide range

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.110
of negative effects.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.000
China's unemployment rate is picking up,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.010
especially for young people who are some

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.713
of the biggest consumers
of American-made products.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.120
The unemployment rate for
people aged 16 to 24 has doubled

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.500
over the past four years

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.010
and rose to 21% in June,
the highest level ever.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.840
China's government suspended the survey

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.630
after June's record reading
and has cut off data releases

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.930
for corporate registration
information, patents, and more.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.870
The countries yuan currency
also fell to its lowest level

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.660
in 16 years against the dollar last month.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.130
That means products sold in China

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.980
will be more expensive for local consumers

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.710
or they'll have to be
marked down in dollar terms,

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.650
which means less money
comes back to US companies.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.050
Companies may still be
able to hit their targets

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.120
despite these headwinds from China

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.620
but get ready to hear a lot more

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.172
about them in the coming weeks.

00:03:03.172 --> 00:03:05.922
(dramatic music)

